  "reason": "The study reports on high-throughput screening of mouse gene knockouts and identifies phenotypes. While it mentions that mouse gene knockout obesity predicts association with human orthologous genes, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity, specificity) between the mouse knockout results and human clinical results. The comparison to IMPC data is for validation of mouse phenotypes, not for agreement with human outcomes."
